        "original_id": "c6646312-b826-5d5d-9926-d67674b1f6c6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Francine McDougall, Marley Shelton, Marla Sokoloff, Mena Suvari, James Marsden, Melissa George\n- Products: Sugar & Spice, Go Figure, Cow Belles\n- Roles: film director, film producer, photographer, television director, television producer, screenwriter\n- Topics: feature film directorial debut, teen crime comedy film\n\nFacts:\n- Francine McDougall is an Australian film director, film producer, photographer, television director, television producer, and screenwriter.\n- In 2001, Francine McDougall made her feature film directorial debut with the comedy film Sugar & Spice.\n- Sugar & Spice is a 2001 American teen crime comedy film directed by Francine McDougall and starring Marley Shelton, Marla Sokoloff, Mena Suvari, James Marsden, and Melissa George.\n- Sugar & Spice follows a group of high school cheerleaders who plan and carry out an armed robbery after one of them becomes pregnant and needs money.\n- Francine McDougall also directed the Disney Channel Original Movies Go Figure in 2005 and Cow Belles in 2006.",
